# NOTICE — provenance and third-party references

`dsh-account-hub` is a **fork** of
[`dsh-plugin-subscriptions`](https://github.com/V1ki/dsh-plugin-subscriptions)
(v0.9.10, MIT) by **V1ki** and its contributors. The upstream copyright and
MIT license are preserved in `LICENSE`. All upstream subscription providers,
their OAuth flows, translation layers, account pool, model catalog store,
settings page and tests remain under that license; this fork adds the account
and quota work described in `docs/opencode-go.md` and the repository history.

## Design and protocol references

The OpenCode Go integration was designed from the following public projects
and data. No unmodified source files were copied from them; protocol shapes,
endpoint layout and operational policy were re-implemented for this fork:

- [`Duskriver/dsh-opencode-go`](https://github.com/Duskriver/dsh-opencode-go)
  (MIT) — OpenCode Go provider identity, `x-opencode-session` routing header,
  multi-protocol gateway layout (`/openai/v1`, `/anthropic`), 5h/weekly/monthly
  usage contract and account failover semantics.
- [`grikomsn/pi-provider-opencode-console`](https://github.com/grikomsn/pi-provider-opencode-console)
  (MIT) — OpenCode Console/Go OAuth device-code reference (future option;
  not enabled by default in this fork).
- [`Aa728848/dsh-chatgpt-subscription`](https://github.com/Aa728848/dsh-chatgpt-subscription)
  (MIT) — multi-provider subscription line layout, shared account-pool kernel,
  "adopted snapshot is never refreshed" import policy, DPAPI storage guidance.
- [`franksong2702/dsh-codex-connect`](https://github.com/franksong2702/dsh-codex-connect)
  (Apache-2.0) — account-document migration/validation, quota wait/rotation
  state machines, masked account labels.
- `@earendil-works/pi-ai` provider data (`opencode-go.json`, models.dev-derived)
  — the static model catalog snapshot in `data/opencode-go.json`, regenerated
  into `src/providers/opencode-models.ts`.
- `dsh-cost-meter` documentation — quota endpoint/source inventory used only as
  a reference; this fork does not ship a billing ledger.

